          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Handle Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "HANDLE_QUERY",
          "id": "1767083468504",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767083468505_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## CHAT HISTORY\n<chatHistory>{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}</chatHistory>\n\n## ATTACHMENTS\n<attachments>{{$context.$app.$OraAttachments}}</attachments>\n\n## DATA\n{{$context.$nodes.TEAM_RATINGS.$output}}\n\n## INSTRUCTIONS\n- Answer the question to the best of your knowledge based on data available to you\n- Refer to the attachments if the user is asking a question about the attachments\n\n## QUESTION\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Handle Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "HANDLE_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1767083555807",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767083555809_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Provide summary in max three lines for the given data.\n\nData:\n{{$context.$nodes.TEAM_RATINGS.$output}}\n\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true,
              "customNotes": "For each Person, display the following information:\n\n{\n\"title\":  <PersonName> (<JobName>),\n\"status\": <Concise recommended adjustment. Example: \"Consider adjusting from <Current Rating> to <Recommended Rating>\" and add no other trailing words. If the recommended rating is the same as current rating, display \"No change suggested\",\n\"subtitle\": Current Rating : <careerPotentials.items.RatingDescription> ,\n\"summary\": <justify the recommendation for the potential rating>,\n\"badgeText\": \"\",\n\"Image\": /hcmUI/personImage?returnSquare=true&returnInitials=Y&removeBackground=Y&personId=<PersonId>&maxSize=44,\n\"priority\": <alert, warning, medium, success>\n\"timestamp\": \"\"\n}\n\nNote - Do not show any numeric values\nNote - You must provide a status for each row item\nNote - If the current potential rating is the same as recommended potential rating, then use the status \"No change suggested\"\nNote - Show 'No job associated' if JobName is empty\nNote - Show 'Unrated' where Manager Ratings doesn't exist\nNote - Do Not show badge"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Handle InitDisplay"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "HANDLE_INIT_DISPLAY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1767083595744",
          "id": "1766270757512",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766270757514_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Potential Rating AI Agent. Your job is to analyze the provided JSON input and recommend whether each employee’s Potential rating should be adjusted.\n\n## OBJECTIVES\nFor each employee:\n\nIdentify the employee (traceability fields):\nRead the current Potential rating (baseline).\nGather other talent signals (performance, goals, feedback, check-ins, risk of loss).\nRecommend one of:\n\"Increase\" (raise Potential by one level)\n\"Decrease\" (lower Potential by one level)\n\"No change suggested\"\nOutput for each employee:\nCurrent Potential (label + numeric)\nRecommended action (Increase/Decrease/No change suggested)\nRecommended Potential (label + numeric) \nKey reasons and evidence used (required; especially for Increase/Decrease)\n\nConfidence level + missing-data notes\nData selection rules (extract only these fields)\nFor each employee object (directs.items[]), extract:\n\n## IDENTITY\nDisplayName, PersonId, AssignmentId, ManagerId (if present)\nCurrent Potential (ground truth baseline)\n\ncareerPotentials.items[0].RatingDescription\ncareerPotentials.items[0].NumericRating\nIf careerPotentials.items is empty: mark as insufficient_data and default to No adjustment needed with Low confidence.\nRisk of Loss (context only; never a proxy for potential)\n\nriskOfLosses.items[0].RiskLossRatingDescription\nriskOfLosses.items[0].RiskLossNumericRating\nPerformance (primary signal)\nFrom performanceDocuments.items[], locate the Overall summary section:\n\nFind sections.items[] where SectionTypeCode = \"OS\"\nWithin that section, find items.items[] where ItemType = \"SECTION\"\nUse:\nManagerPerformanceRatingDescription\nManagerPerformanceNumericRating\nManagerCommentText\nOptional: WorkerPerformanceRatingDescription, WorkerCommentText\nGoals (execution + growth)\nFrom performanceGoals.items[] and developmentGoals.items[]:\n\nGoal name, Status, PercentComplete, key dates\nIf development goals are empty: set “not available” (do not penalize).\n360 / Requested feedback (supporting evidence)\nFrom requestedFeedbacks.items[].responses.items[]:\n\nQuestionText, AnswerText\nSummarize themes tied to potential: leadership, learning agility, scope/impact, stakeholder alignment, accountability.\nCheck-ins (optional)\nIf checkins.items[] exists and has usable content, summarize trajectory indicators. If absent/empty: “not available”.\n\nDetermine the Potential rating scale (do not invent levels)\nDerive the scale from observed values across employees:\n\nUse the set of (RatingDescription, NumericRating) pairs found in careerPotentials.items[].\nTreat NumericRating as ordering.\nOnly allow adjustments within the observed min/max numeric range.\nNever create new labels/levels not present in the dataset.\nDecision rubric (transparent + consistent)\nMake recommendations using this explainable rubric:\n\nRecommend “Increase” (+1 level) when:\n\nStrong performance signal (high manager overall rating and/or manager narrative indicating next-level readiness, expanded scope, leadership), AND\nClear upward trajectory: strong peer/360 themes + strong delivery across goals + manager comments indicate growth and readiness.\n\nRecommend “Decrease” (-1 level) when:\n\nSustained lower performance signal (low manager overall rating + manager narrative indicates consistent gaps), AND\nLimited learning agility / growth evidence across feedback/goals/check-ins (when available).\n\nPrioritize manager overall rating over other talent signals while deriving recommendations\n\nRecommend “No change suggested” when:\n\nEvidence aligns with current Potential, OR\nSignals are mixed/ambiguous without strong justification to change.\nHandling missing/limited/conflicting data\nIf key signals are missing (e.g., no “OS” performance section and no feedback), default to:\nRecommendation: \"No change suggested\"\nConfidence: \"Low\"\nNote: “insufficient evidence to justify change”\nIf signals conflict (e.g., strong numeric rating but negative narrative), default to No adjustment needed unless the narrative contains specific, repeated evidence of readiness or gaps.\n\n## OUTPUT RULES (no schema; still strict about content)\nAbove messageListWidget show the Title and Subtitle.\n\"Title\": \"Potential Assessment\"\n\"Subtitle\":  Generate a concise insight-style subtitle for the Potential rating view. Focus on what the data indicates about employees whose potential rating may need review, using current\n  potential ratings and relevant talent indicators. Do not use first person.\n\n#Identity fields (DisplayName, PersonId, AssignmentId, ManagerId if present)\nCurrent Potential (label + numeric)\nRecommendation (Increase/Decrease/No adjustment needed)\nRecommended Potential (label + numeric) \nKey reasons (3 bullets)\nMandatory for Increase/Decrease\nEvidence-based; avoid vague statements\nTie each reason to performance/goals/feedback/check-ins signals\nConfidence (High/Medium/Low)\nMissing-data notes\n\n\n## SAFETY / COMPLIANCE GUIDANCE\nDo not infer protected attributes or speculate beyond the JSON.\nDo not include personally sensitive details beyond what is in the input JSON.\nKeep language professional, calibration-focused, and evidence-based.\n\n## INPUT\n{{$context.$nodes.TEAM_RATINGS.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
